  body: "# Entitlement and payability of a retained child dependency increase\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\
    \nThe captured guidance separates entitlement to a child dependency increase from its payability:
    the child-benefit and exclusion conditions are distinguished from treated-as-living-with or maintenance
    conditions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThese are retained dependency provisions in the chapter’s
    savings, transitional or unaffected-benefit scope. Child Benefit receipt alone does not establish
    payment, and living together alone does not establish entitlement. Current rates, maintenance calculation,
    family definitions and all exclusions remain unresolved.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG
    16000, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16029, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16030, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16033, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch16`: PDF SHA-256 `98d3f27a839795c416988c7a5770c403b8f046be78de244feaf612e4515ac3ed`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `7d8c71fa0ff5bbf0e45ab1044c34ebd8cb9bac48f582b20924e3ba78fd12fe5d`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
