    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter warns that much of the dependency text is retained for transitional and
      unaffected cases; the entitlement/payability distinction must remain inside that scope.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch16/0009
      quote: "16000   Certain CDIs have been abolished1. DMG 16003 -16013 provides guidance on this\n\
        \        and on the transitional and savings arrangements2. The guidance on CDIs in DMG\n    \
        \    16015 et seq is retained for transitional cases and benefits not affected (see DMG\n    \
        \    16002).\n                                                                 1 TC Act 02, s
        1(3)(e); 2 TC Comm No. 3 Order, art. 3\n\n\n        Benefits affected"
      locator: DMG 16000
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch16/0015
      quote: "16029   DMs should note the difference between entitlement1 and payability. Although benefit\n\
        \        may not be payable, entitlement may remain2.\n                                      \
        \                       1 [1984] 1 WLR 1353; 2 SS CB Act 92, s 122(1)\n\n\n        Entitlement"
      locator: DMG 16029
